    summary: "Many carry wounds from childhood or family history. This lesson studies Exodus 20:5-6, Ezekiel 18:14-20, Genesis 37, Genesis 45:1-8 and Psalm 78:5-8 to see that sin and hurt can echo across generations, that each person is responsible for their own choices, that God breaks cycles, and how to forgive parents, siblings and family members, set boundaries, and build new patterns.",
    scripture: ["Ezekiel 18:14-20", "Psalm 78:5-8"], more: ["Exodus 20:5-6", "Genesis 37:3-4", "Genesis 45:1-8"], memory: "Ezekiel 18:20",
